WEBVTT

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.160
Hi again, it's Pinky!

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:05.760
Two equations, two unknowns.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.560
It looks like double the work.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.920
It's not. Watch one letter vanish.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:15.060
You're allowed to add two equations together,

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:16.360
or subtract them.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:17.860
If both are true,

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:19.440
the sum is true too,

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:21.260
and the solution stays the same.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.320
And when the letters are set up right,

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.060
one of them just cancels.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.040
Look. X plus y equals twelve.

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.680
X minus y equals four.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.340
See the plus y,

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:34.440
and the minus y?

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.880
They're opposites. That's the signal.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.500
Add them, straight down.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:41.580
X plus x is two x.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.560
Plus y, minus y:

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.420
gone! Twelve plus four is sixteen.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:48.920
Two x equals sixteen,

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:50.020
so x is eight.

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:51.600
Put eight back in.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:53.080
Eight plus y is twelve,

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.480
so y is four.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:58.680
Your turn. X plus y equals ten.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:00.920
X minus y equals two.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:02.420
What is x?

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:04.880
I'll wait.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.120
Six! Add them,

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:14.860
and you get two x equals twelve.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.100
X is six.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:18.880
Before you do anything,

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:21.180
look for matching or opposite coefficients.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:23.760
Matching? Subtract. Opposite?

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:25.560
Add. That's the whole scan.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:28.040
And on the SAT,

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:30.360
you can also graph both equations.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:31.760
Where the lines cross,

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:33.140
that's your solution.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.620
But a graph window can hide a crossing.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:37.960
Zoom in the wrong place,

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:39.740
and the lines look like they never meet.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.380
So check your point in both of the original equations.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:46.720
A point on only one line is not a solution.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.840
So: scan for matching or opposite terms.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:52.180
Add or subtract.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:53.860
Then check both equations.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:55.800
Now hit Try this skill,

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.400
and go make some letters vanish!
